QZip's default compression engine (`src/engine_mcmfork/`, built as `src/native/qzmf`) is a fork of mcm:

  mcm file compressor, version 0.84, upstream commit 1c44c95
  https://github.com/mathieuchartier/mcm
  Copyright (C) 2013, Google Inc. Author: Mathieu Chartier
  GNU General Public License v3 or later (src/engine_mcmfork/COPYING)

Every original mcm copyright and license header is kept unchanged. The QZip changes (2026, Elliott Hankinson) — the
table and text models that produce the size gains — are listed in src/engine_mcmfork/QZIP_FORK.md; in short:
  * QzCsv.hpp (new): an adaptive CSV/TSV tracker (delimiter and field count learned from coded bytes only);
  * table contexts (field index, byte/field above, previous field) and a field-indexed mixer select;
  * a new level -q (archive type kTypeCMQz) with three text contexts from QZip's x18 design;
  * build fixes for GCC 13 and a benchmark script (src/engine_mcmfork/bench/).
Archives made with the -q level, or tables made by the fork, are not decodable by stock mcm.

Because the default engine is GPL, QZip as distributed in this repository is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.

Other third-party components (libbsc, libsais: Apache-2.0; stock mcm 0.84 for the legacy max/ultra modes: GPL-3.0-or-
later; lpaq1 by Matt Mahoney: GPL-2.0-or-later) are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
